# Initial Vertical Slice

Implement one chart:

## Real GDP Growth

The chart must use an authoritative public economic-data source.

For this epic, use FRED as the external provider unless access problems make that impractical.

Use a real GDP series appropriate for showing U.S. economic growth. The implementation must document the selected series identifier and why it was selected.

The default chart should show real GDP growth as a year-over-year percentage change.

The chart must not calculate growth from nominal GDP.

If the upstream source already provides the desired transformation reliably, the application may request that transformation. Otherwise, calculate it in the application’s normalization layer and test the calculation.

