# Chart Requirements

The chart must:

- Render real data
- Use dates on the horizontal axis
- Use percentage growth on the vertical axis
- Include a zero reference line
- Provide an accessible tooltip
- Display exact observation period and value in the tooltip
- Handle missing values without connecting misleading lines
- Resize responsively
- Avoid 3D effects
- Avoid decorative gradients
- Avoid truncated axes that exaggerate small changes
- Avoid smoothing that implies nonexistent observations

Provide time-range controls:

- 5 years
- 10 years
- 20 years
- Maximum available

The default should be 20 years unless the available data makes another choice clearly better.

Do not add recession shading in this epic unless it can be implemented cleanly without delaying the foundational work. The chart architecture should permit future annotation bands.

The chart must have a textual accessible summary or equivalent screen-reader support. A canvas-only chart without accessible fallback is not acceptable.

