# Security Requirements

- Keep FRED and Supabase privileged credentials server-side.
- Never expose service-role credentials to the browser.
- Validate all endpoint inputs.
- Restrict allowed series identifiers or slugs.
- Do not accept arbitrary provider URLs from client input.
- Do not commit `.env` files.
- Do not log secrets.
- Use least-privilege database access where practical.
- Document any security compromises made for the initial version.

---

# Performance Requirements

For the initial GDP series:

- Avoid sending unnecessary provider metadata to the browser.
- Return observations in chronological order.
- Cache API responses where appropriate.
- Avoid refetch loops.
- Do not rerender or recreate the full chart unnecessarily.
- Keep the initial client bundle reasonable.
- Lazy-load the charting library if doing so materially improves initial loading without excessive complexity.

No premature generalized optimization framework is required.

