# Implementation Constraints

- Do not call FRED directly from React.
- Do not hardcode chart observations.
- Do not put secrets in the browser.
- Do not silently treat missing data as zero.
- Do not use `any` to bypass domain modeling.
- Do not mix external-provider response types with client-facing API types.
- Do not create a generic dashboard builder.
- Do not create a plugin system.
- Do not implement authentication.
- Do not add Redux unless a demonstrated state-management requirement justifies it.
- Do not add a large component framework unless it provides clear value.
- Do not add multiple economic series to make the page appear fuller.
- Do not represent the economy with a single health score.
- Do not present a percentage without clearly identifying the transformation and period.

